<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution makes Finland a republic, with K. J. Ståhlberg as president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-raj"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Raj.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Raj</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Troops kill hundreds of unarmed people at the Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/chavin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Chav%C3%ADn.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Chavín</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Julio C. Tello begins work at the site and calls Chavín the mother culture of the Andes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/indian-independence-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indian%20independence%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indian independence movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Troops fire on an unarmed crowd at Jallianwala Bagh in Amritsar, killing hundreds</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/labour-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Labour%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Labour movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The International Labour Organization is founded under the Treaty of Versailles</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/pan-africanism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Africanism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Africanism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Du Bois’s first Pan-African Congress meets in Paris during the peace conference</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/ubaid-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ubaid%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ubaid culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Henry Hall begins the first large excavation of Ubaid material at Tell al-ʿUbaid</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/bauhaus"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bauhaus.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bauhaus</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Walter Gropius founds the Bauhaus in Weimar, merging the Grand Ducal Saxon Academy of Fine Art and the Grand Ducal Saxon School of Arts and Crafts</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/may-fourth-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/May%20Fourth%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>May Fourth Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On May 4 over 4,000 students gather in front of Tiananmen to protest the Shandong terms of the Treaty of Versailles</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/may-fourth-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/May%20Fourth%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>May Fourth Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the June 3 arrests a general strike in Shanghai forces the dismissal of Cao Rulin, Zhang Zongxiang and Lu Zongyu, and China’s delegates refuse to sign the treaty</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/harlem-renaissance"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Harlem%20Renaissance.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Harlem Renaissance</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Claude McKay publishes his militant sonnet “If We Must Die” in the year of the Red Summer</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/communism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Communism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Communism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks found the Comintern, dedicated to promoting revolution throughout the world</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/social-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Social%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Social democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the German Revolution the Social Democrats defend what becomes the Weimar Republic against Communists seeking a soviet republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/maoism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Maoism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Maoism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The May Fourth Movement begins with 3,000 students in Beijing protesting the Versailles Treaty’s concessions to Japan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/fascism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Fascism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Fascism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mussolini founds the Italian Fasces of Combat in Milan, and the Fascist Manifesto is published</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/feminism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Feminism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Feminism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Nineteenth Amendment grants American women the vote in all states, closing the first wave in the United States</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/divine-comedy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Divine%20Comedy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Divine Comedy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Miguel Asín Palacios argues for Islamic sources of the poem in La Escatología musulmana en la Divina Comedia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-state-of-prussia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20State%20of%20Prussia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free State of Prussia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Prussian State Assembly is elected on 26 January and the Weimar Coalition forms a government in March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania-1918-1940"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Lithuania%20(1918-1940).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Lithuania (1918-1940)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The government moves to Kaunas, and by the end of August the Soviets are pushed out of Lithuanian territory</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/ukrainian-ssr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ukrainian%20SSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ukrainian SSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Third All-Ukrainian Congress of Soviets ratified the Constitution of the Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic in Kharkiv</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/weimar-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Weimar%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Weimar Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Women vote for the first time in the election to the National Assembly, which then meets in Weimar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/weimar-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Weimar%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Weimar Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany signs the Treaty of Versailles</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-east-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20East%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German East Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Paris Peace Conference awards the colony to Britain, which cedes Ruanda and Urundi to Belgium, while the Kionga Triangle goes to Portugal</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/korea-under-japanese-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Korea%20under%20Japanese%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Korea under Japanese rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After Emperor Gojong's sudden death, the March First Movement brings an estimated 2 million people to peaceful rallies, which Japan violently suppresses</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/second-polish-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Second%20Polish%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Second Polish Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Versailles confirms the rebirth of Poland, and the Small Constitution of 1919 establishes a parliamentary democracy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/mustafa-kemal-ataturk"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mustafa%20Kemal%20Atat%C3%BCrk.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lands at Samsun on 19 May to organise a national movement against the occupation and issues the Amasya Circular</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/medina"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Medina.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Medina</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Sharifate of Mecca takes the city after the siege that began in 1916</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kabul"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kabul.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kabul</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Amanullah Khan announces Afghanistan's independence in foreign affairs at the Eidgah Mosque</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mohenjo-daro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mohenjo-daro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mohenjo-daro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">R. D. Banerji visits the site, finds a flint scraper and is convinced of its antiquity</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/palace-of-versailles"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Palace%20of%20Versailles.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Palace of Versailles</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Treaty of Versailles, ending the First World War, was signed in the Hall of Mirrors</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/albert-einstein"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Albert%20Einstein.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Albert Einstein</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Eddington's observations of the solar eclipse of 29 May give results consistent with his calculations, and the press reports them worldwide</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/rabindranath-tagore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rabindranath%20Tagore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rabindranath Tagore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Renounces his knighthood after the Jallianwala Bagh massacre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/march-first-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/March%20First%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>March First Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Former emperor Gojong dies on 21 January, and Koreans widely suspect that Japan poisoned him</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/march-first-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/March%20First%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>March First Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Students in Japan proclaim a declaration of independence in February and are arrested en masse</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/march-first-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/March%20First%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>March First Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Signers read the Korean Declaration of Independence at T’aehwagwan on 1 March, and a crowd at Tapgol Park begins a march along Jongno</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/march-first-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/March%20First%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>March First Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the Jeamni massacre on 15 April, Japanese authorities lure 20 to 30 civilians into a church, shoot them and burn it down</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/march-first-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/March%20First%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>March First Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Korean exiles in Shanghai found the Korean Provisional Government in April</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Students in Beijing protest the transfer of German rights over Jiaozhou Bay to Japan, and the movement becomes political</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The death of the student Li Chao becomes a rallying cry for anti-feudal and feminist agitation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/nazism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The German Workers’ Party, the Nazi Party’s precursor, is founded</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/christian-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Christian%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Christian democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Poland's Christian democratic movements coalesce into the Christian Democratic Party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/syndicalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syndicalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syndicalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Free Workers' Union of Germany (FAUD) is formed in December</span></li></ul></section>
